/-!
# Solution modules of block relations and determinants of arrays

Let `O` be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field `K`, `𝒜` an `O`-algebra, `ψ : 𝒜 → M_n(O)`
a surjective `O`-algebra homomorphism and `Rel ⊆ 𝒜^ι` a left `𝒜`-submodule (`ι`, `n` finite). An
array `Θ : M_ι(𝒜)` with rows in `Rel` gives the block matrix `ψ(Θ) ∈ M_{ι × n}(O)` with blocks
`ψ(Θ r q)`. The *solution module* is

`Sol = {u ∈ ((K/O)^n)^ι : ∑ q, ψ(θ q) u_q = 0 for all θ ∈ Rel}`.

For one block, every array with rows in `Rel` has `v(det ψ(Θ)) ≥ length Sol`, some array has
equality, and so the ideal generated by these determinants has colength `length Sol` (all three
read in `ℕ∞`, both sides infinite together).

For several surjections `ψ_b : 𝒜 → M_{n_b}(O)`, `b ∈ B`, with solution modules `Sol_b`, an ideal
`J ⊆ O` containing every coefficient of the generic products `∏_b det ψ_b(∑_k X_k Θ_k)`, over all
families of arrays `Θ_k` with rows in `Rel`, has colength at most `∑_b length Sol_b`. If the
residue field of `O` has more than `#ι · ∑_b n_b` elements, it suffices that `J` contains the
products `∏_b det ψ_b(Θ)` for single arrays `Θ`.

The proof has two steps. (Morita) Since `ψ` is onto `M_n(O)` and `Rel` is a left `𝒜`-module, the
rows of all the `ψ(θ)`, `θ ∈ Rel`, read as vectors in `O^{ι × n}`, span a submodule
`R = TauCeti.blockRowSpan ψ Rel`, and any `n` vectors of `R` are the `n` rows of one `ψ(θ)`
(`TauCeti.exists_mem_blockRow_eq`). The solution module is the orthogonal of `R` in
`(K/O)^{ι × n}`, so by Matlis duality its length is the colength of `R`
(`IsDiscreteValuationRing.length_orthogonalBilin`). (Determinants) The rows of `ψ(Θ)` lie in `R`, so
the colength of `R` is at most that of the span of the rows, which is `v(det ψ(Θ))`
(`Matrix.length_quotient_span_range_eq_addVal_det`); conversely, if `R` has finite colength it is
spanned by the rows of a square matrix, whose rows, grouped `n` at a time, are the rows of the
`ψ(θ)` for an array `Θ`.

For several blocks, take for each block an array `Θ_b` with `v(det ψ_b(Θ_b)) = length Sol_b` and
the generic array `∑_b X_b Θ_b`. Write `F_b = det ψ_b(∑_k X_k Θ_k)` as `ϖ^{c_b} G_b` with `G_b` of
unit content; then `c_b ≤ v(F_b(e_b)) = v(det ψ_b(Θ_b))`, and by Gauss's lemma some coefficient of
`∏_b F_b` has valuation `∑_b c_b`. Over a large residue field, the reduction of `∏_b G_b` modulo
`ϖ` is a nonzero polynomial of total degree at most `#ι · ∑_b n_b`, so it does not vanish at some
point of the residue field (combinatorial Nullstellensatz); for a lift `a` of that point the single
array `Θ = ∑_k a_k Θ_k` has `∏_b det ψ_b(Θ) = ϖ^{∑_b c_b}` times a unit. No finite generation of
`Rel` is needed.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.blockSolutions`: the solution module `Sol ⊆ (E^n)^ι` of `Rel` through `ψ`, for any
  `O`-module `E`.
* `TauCeti.blockRowSpan`: the span `R ⊆ O^{ι × n}` of the rows of the block rows `ψ(θ)`, `θ ∈ Rel`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.length_blockSolutions`: `length Sol = length_O (O^{ι × n} / R)`.
* `TauCeti.length_blockSolutions_le_addVal_det`: `length Sol ≤ v(det ψ(Θ))` for every array `Θ`
  with rows in `Rel`.
* `TauCeti.exists_addVal_det_eq_length_blockSolutions`: some array with rows in `Rel` has
  `v(det ψ(Θ)) = length Sol`.
* `TauCeti.length_quotient_span_det_eq_length_blockSolutions`: the ideal generated by the
  determinants of arrays with rows in `Rel` has colength `length Sol`.
* `TauCeti.length_quot_le_sum_length_blockSolutions`: several blocks, an ideal containing the
  coefficients of the generic products of block determinants has colength at most
  `∑_b length Sol_b`.
* `TauCeti.length_quot_le_sum_length_blockSolutions_of_card_residueField`: over a residue field
  with more than `#ι · ∑_b n_b` elements, an ideal containing the products of block determinants
  of single arrays has colength at most `∑_b length Sol_b`.

## Provenance

The inequality `v(det ψ(Θ)) ≤ length Sol` for some array, with `Sol` on `(O/p)ⁿ` and on `(K/O)ⁿ`,
is `New.Selmer.exists_rows_addVal_det_le` and `New.Selmer.exists_rows_addVal_det_le_of_divisible`
in grh-lean (https://github.com/lsernau/grh-lean, file
`src/Lib/General/Algebra/BlockFittingBound.lean`, Apache 2.0, Copyright 2026 Anthropic, PBC). Its
proof is the source of the Morita step here (summing the rows of `ψ(t)`, and the lifts of the
matrices with one row of ones). The equality and the lower bound for every array are new.

The form over a large residue field, with the hypothesis `#ι · ∑_b n_b < #k`, is modelled on
`Formalism.NG.genericFin` in L. Alpöge's Lean formalization of the Riemann hypothesis project
(https://github.com/leanprover-community/riemann-hypothesis, file
`src/Formalism/CharacterColumnKernels/IdempotentNormalForms/GenFin.lean`), which proves, under the
same hypothesis, that a single combination of the relations realizes the kernel lengths of all
blocks at once, through a non-root of a reduced generic determinant found by the combinatorial
Nullstellensatz. The statement here as a colength bound for an ideal of determinants, and its
derivation from the generic multi-block bound by Gauss's lemma, are new.

## References

* K. A. Ribet, *A modular construction of unramified p-extensions of Q(μ_p)*, Invent. Math. 34
  (1976), §§2–4, where determinants of such block arrays bound congruence ideals.
-/

public section

open IsDiscreteValuationRing Matrix LinearMap

namespace TauCeti

variable {O : Type*} [CommRing O] {𝒜 : Type*} [Ring 𝒜] [Algebra O 𝒜]
  {ι n : Type*} [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n]

section Defs

variable (ψ : 𝒜 →ₐ[O] Matrix n n O) (Rel : Submodule 𝒜 (ι → 𝒜))

/-- The solution module of the relations `Rel ⊆ 𝒜^ι` through `ψ : 𝒜 → M_n(O)` with values in an
`O`-module `E`: the `u ∈ (E^n)^ι` with `∑ q, ψ(θ q) u_q = 0` for every `θ ∈ Rel`, where the
matrices act on `E^n` by multiplication. -/
def blockSolutions [Fintype ι] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module O E] :
    Submodule O (ι → n → E) :=
  ⨅ θ ∈ Rel, ⨅ i : n, LinearMap.ker (∑ q : ι, ∑ j : n, ψ (θ q) i j •
    ((LinearMap.proj j : (n → E) →ₗ[O] E) ∘ₗ (LinearMap.proj q : (ι → n → E) →ₗ[O] n → E)))

@[simp]
theorem mem_blockSolutions [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [AddCommGroup E] [Module O E] {u : ι → n → E} :
    u ∈ blockSolutions ψ Rel E ↔ ∀ θ ∈ Rel, ∀ i, ∑ q, ∑ j, ψ (θ q) i j • u q j = 0 := by
  simp [blockSolutions]

/-- The span in `O^{ι × n}` of the rows of the block rows `ψ(θ) = (ψ(θ q))_q`, `θ ∈ Rel`: row `i`
of `ψ(θ)` is the vector `(q, j) ↦ ψ(θ q) i j`. -/
def blockRowSpan : Submodule O (ι × n → O) :=
  Submodule.span O {v | ∃ θ ∈ Rel, ∃ i : n, v = fun qj ↦ ψ (θ qj.1) i qj.2}

theorem blockRow_mem_blockRowSpan {θ : ι → 𝒜} (hθ : θ ∈ Rel) (i : n) :
    (fun qj : ι × n ↦ ψ (θ qj.1) i qj.2) ∈ blockRowSpan ψ Rel :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨θ, hθ, i, rfl⟩

/-- The solution module with values in `E` is the orthogonal of the row span, after currying
`E^{ι × n} = (E^n)^ι`. -/
theorem blockSolutions_eq_map_orthogonalBilin [Fintype ι] (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E]
    [Module O E] :
    blockSolutions ψ Rel E =
      ((blockRowSpan ψ Rel).orthogonalBilin (Fintype.bilinearCombination O O (M := E)).flip).map
        (LinearEquiv.curry O E ι n).toLinearMap := by
  ext u
  rw [Submodule.mem_map_equiv, blockRowSpan, Submodule.mem_orthogonalBilin_span,
    mem_blockSolutions]
  simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, forall_exists_index, and_imp]
  refine ⟨fun h v θ hθ i hv ↦ ?_, fun h θ hθ i ↦ ?_⟩
  · subst hv
    simpa [Fintype.linearCombination_apply, Fintype.sum_prod_type] using h θ hθ i
  · simpa [Fintype.linearCombination_apply, Fintype.sum_prod_type] using h θ hθ i rfl

end Defs

section Morita

variable (ψ : 𝒜 →ₐ[O] Matrix n n O) (Rel : Submodule 𝒜 (ι → 𝒜))

/-- The sum of the rows of the block row `ψ(t)`, as a vector of `O^{ι × n}`. -/
private def rowSum : (ι → 𝒜) →ₗ[O] (ι × n → O) :=
  LinearMap.pi fun qj ↦ ∑ c, entryLinearMap O O c qj.2 ∘ₗ ψ.toLinearMap ∘ₗ LinearMap.proj qj.1

private theorem rowSum_apply (t : ι → 𝒜) (qj : ι × n) :
    rowSum ψ t qj = ∑ c, ψ (t qj.1) c qj.2 := by
  simp [rowSum]

/-- If `ψ` is surjective, the row span is the set of row sums of elements of `Rel`. -/
private theorem blockRowSpan_eq_map (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) :
    blockRowSpan ψ Rel = (Rel.restrictScalars O).map (rowSum ψ) := by
  refine le_antisymm (Submodule.span_le.2 ?_) (Submodule.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 fun t ht ↦ ?_)
  · -- Row `i` of `ψ(θ)` is the row sum of `e θ`, with `ψ(e)` the matrix unit at `(i, i)`.
    rintro _ ⟨θ, hθ, i, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hψ (single i i 1)
    refine ⟨e • θ, Rel.smul_mem e hθ, funext fun qj ↦ ?_⟩
    simp [rowSum_apply, he, Matrix.mul_apply, Matrix.single_apply, ite_and]
  · -- A row sum is a sum of rows.
    have h : rowSum ψ t = ∑ c, fun qj : ι × n ↦ ψ (t qj.1) c qj.2 := by
      ext qj
      simp [rowSum_apply]
    rw [Submodule.mem_comap, h]
    exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun c _ ↦ blockRow_mem_blockRowSpan ψ Rel ht c

/-- **Morita step.** If `ψ` is surjective, any `n` vectors `v i` of the row span are the rows of
one block row: there is `θ ∈ Rel` with `ψ(θ q) i j = v i (q, j)`. -/
theorem exists_mem_blockRow_eq (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) {v : n → ι × n → O}
    (hv : ∀ i, v i ∈ blockRowSpan ψ Rel) :
    ∃ θ ∈ Rel, ∀ i q j, ψ (θ q) i j = v i (q, j) := by
  rw [blockRowSpan_eq_map ψ Rel hψ] at hv
  choose t ht hvt using hv
  -- `ψ(e c)` has ones in row `c` and zeros elsewhere, so row `c` of `ψ(e c • t c)` sums the rows.
  choose e he using fun c : n ↦ hψ (of fun i (_ : n) ↦ if i = c then (1 : O) else 0)
  refine ⟨∑ c, e c • t c, Rel.sum_mem fun c _ ↦ Rel.smul_mem _ (ht c), fun i q j ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [← hvt i, rowSum_apply]
  simp [Finset.sum_apply, he, Matrix.mul_apply, Matrix.sum_apply]

/-- The rows of the block matrix `ψ(Θ)` of an array with rows in `Rel` lie in the row span. -/
theorem span_range_row_comp_le_blockRowSpan {Θ : Matrix ι ι 𝒜} (hΘ : ∀ r, Θ r ∈ Rel) :
    Submodule.span O (Set.range (comp ι ι n n O (Θ.map ψ)).row) ≤ blockRowSpan ψ Rel :=
  Submodule.span_le.2 <| Set.range_subset_iff.2 fun ri ↦
    blockRow_mem_blockRowSpan ψ Rel (hΘ ri.1) ri.2

end Morita

section Lengths

variable [Fintype ι] [IsDomain O] [IsDiscreteValuationRing O] {K : Type*} [Field K] [Algebra O K]
  [IsFractionRing O K] (ψ : 𝒜 →ₐ[O] Matrix n n O) (Rel : Submodule 𝒜 (ι → 𝒜))

/-- **The solution module is dual to the row span.** `Sol ⊆ ((K/O)^n)^ι` has the length of
`O^{ι × n} / R`, `R` the span of the rows of the `ψ(θ)`, `θ ∈ Rel`. -/
theorem length_blockSolutions :
    Module.length O (blockSolutions ψ Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) =
      Module.length O ((ι × n → O) ⧸ blockRowSpan ψ Rel) := by
  rw [blockSolutions_eq_map_orthogonalBilin,
    ← ((LinearEquiv.curry O _ ι n).submoduleMap _).length_eq, length_orthogonalBilin]

variable [DecidableEq ι]

/-- **Lower bound for every array.** If `Θ` is an array over `𝒜` with rows in `Rel`, then
`length Sol ≤ v(det ψ(Θ))`, with `ψ(Θ)` the block matrix with blocks `ψ(Θ r q)`. -/
theorem length_blockSolutions_le_addVal_det {Θ : Matrix ι ι 𝒜} (hΘ : ∀ r, Θ r ∈ Rel) :
    Module.length O (blockSolutions ψ Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) ≤
      addVal O (comp ι ι n n O (Θ.map ψ)).det := by
  rw [length_blockSolutions, ← length_quotient_span_range_eq_addVal_det]
  exact length_quotient_anti (span_range_row_comp_le_blockRowSpan ψ Rel hΘ)

/-- **An optimal array.** If `ψ` is surjective, some array `Θ` with rows in `Rel` has
`v(det ψ(Θ)) = length Sol`. -/
theorem exists_addVal_det_eq_length_blockSolutions (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) :
    ∃ Θ : Matrix ι ι 𝒜, (∀ r, Θ r ∈ Rel) ∧ addVal O (comp ι ι n n O (Θ.map ψ)).det =
      Module.length O (blockSolutions ψ Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) := by
  rw [length_blockSolutions]
  -- When the row span has finite colength it is spanned by the rows of a square matrix, whose
  -- rows, `n` at a time, are the rows of block rows `ψ(θ)`; otherwise `Θ = 0` works.
  by_cases htop : Module.length O ((ι × n → O) ⧸ blockRowSpan ψ Rel) = ⊤
  · refine ⟨0, fun _ ↦ Rel.zero_mem, ?_⟩
    rw [htop]
    cases isEmpty_or_nonempty (ι × n)
    · exact absurd htop (by simp [Module.length_eq_zero])
    · have h0 : comp ι ι n n O (0 : Matrix ι ι (Matrix n n O)) = 0 := by
        rw [← compAddEquiv_apply, map_zero]
      simp [h0]
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := exists_matrix_span_range_row_eq _ htop
  have hrow (r : ι) (i : n) : M (r, i) ∈ blockRowSpan ψ Rel :=
    hM ▸ Submodule.subset_span ⟨(r, i), rfl⟩
  choose θ hθ hθM using fun r ↦ exists_mem_blockRow_eq ψ Rel hψ (hrow r)
  have hcomp : comp ι ι n n O ((of θ).map ψ) = M := by
    ext ⟨r, i⟩ ⟨q, j⟩
    simp [hθM]
  refine ⟨of θ, hθ, ?_⟩
  rw [hcomp, ← length_quotient_span_range_eq_addVal_det, hM]

/-- **Lengths from determinants of block arrays, one block.** If `ψ : 𝒜 → M_n(O)` is surjective, the
ideal generated by the determinants of the block matrices `ψ(Θ)` of arrays `Θ` with rows in `Rel`
has colength `length_O Sol`, both sides infinite together. -/
theorem length_quotient_span_det_eq_length_blockSolutions (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) :
    Module.length O (O ⧸ Ideal.span
        {x | ∃ Θ : Matrix ι ι 𝒜, (∀ r, Θ r ∈ Rel) ∧ (comp ι ι n n O (Θ.map ψ)).det = x}) =
      Module.length O (blockSolutions ψ Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) := by
  obtain ⟨Θ₀, hΘ₀, hdet⟩ := exists_addVal_det_eq_length_blockSolutions (K := K) ψ Rel hψ
  have hspan : Ideal.span
      {x | ∃ Θ : Matrix ι ι 𝒜, (∀ r, Θ r ∈ Rel) ∧ (comp ι ι n n O (Θ.map ψ)).det = x} =
      Ideal.span {(comp ι ι n n O (Θ₀.map ψ)).det} := by
    refine le_antisymm (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_) (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_)
    · rintro _ ⟨Θ, hΘ, rfl⟩
      refine Ideal.mem_span_singleton.2 (addVal_le_iff_dvd.1 ?_)
      rw [hdet]
      exact length_blockSolutions_le_addVal_det ψ Rel hΘ
    · rintro _ rfl
      exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨Θ₀, hΘ₀, rfl⟩
  rw [hspan, ← Ring.ord, Ring.ord_eq_addVal, hdet]

end Lengths

section Generic

open MvPolynomial

variable [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [IsDomain O] [IsDiscreteValuationRing O] {K : Type*}
  [Field K] [Algebra O K] [IsFractionRing O K]

omit [Fintype n] [IsDomain O] [IsDiscreteValuationRing O] in
/-- The generic block determinant `det ψ(∑_k X_k Θ_k)` evaluated at `a` is `det ψ(∑_k a_k Θ_k)`. -/
private theorem eval_det_generic [Fintype n] (ψ : 𝒜 →ₐ[O] Matrix n n O) {m : ℕ}
    (Θ : Fin m → Matrix ι ι 𝒜) (a : Fin m → O) :
    eval a (Matrix.of fun (ri qj : ι × n) ↦ ∑ k, X k * C (ψ (Θ k ri.1 qj.1) ri.2 qj.2)).det =
      (comp ι ι n n O ((∑ k, a k • Θ k).map ψ)).det := by
  rw [RingHom.map_det]
  congr 1
  ext ⟨r, i⟩ ⟨q, j⟩
  simp [Matrix.sum_apply]

omit [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n] in
/-- The common part of the proofs of the generic and the large-residue-field bounds. If every
`Sol_b` has finite length, there are arrays `Θ_b` with rows in `Rel` such that the generic block
determinants `F_b = det ψ_b(∑_k X_k Θ_{e⁻¹ k})` factor as `ϖ^{c_b} G_b` with `G_b` of unit content
and `c_b ≤ length Sol_b`. -/
private theorem exists_generic_factorization {B : Type*} [Fintype B] {n : B → Type*}
    [∀ b, Fintype (n b)] [∀ b, DecidableEq (n b)] (ψ : ∀ b, 𝒜 →ₐ[O] Matrix (n b) (n b) O)
    (hψ : ∀ b, Function.Surjective (ψ b)) (Rel : Submodule 𝒜 (ι → 𝒜)) {ϖ : O}
    (hϖ : Irreducible ϖ) (htop : ∀ b, Module.length O
      (blockSolutions (ψ b) Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ (Θ : B → Matrix ι ι 𝒜) (c : B → ℕ) (G : B → MvPolynomial (Fin (Fintype.card B)) O),
      (∀ b r, Θ b r ∈ Rel) ∧ (∀ b, ∃ t, IsUnit ((G b).coeff t)) ∧
      (∀ b, (Matrix.of fun (ri qj : ι × n b) ↦ ∑ k, X k *
        C (ψ b (Θ ((Fintype.equivFin B).symm k) ri.1 qj.1) ri.2 qj.2)).det = C (ϖ ^ c b) * G b) ∧
      ∀ b, (c b : ℕ∞) ≤
        Module.length O (blockSolutions (ψ b) Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) := by
  classical
  choose Θ hΘ hdet using fun b ↦
    exists_addVal_det_eq_length_blockSolutions (K := K) (ψ b) Rel (hψ b)
  let e := Fintype.equivFin B
  -- At the `b`-th coordinate vector, `F b` is the determinant of the optimal array of block `b`.
  have hF (b : B) : eval (Pi.single (e b) 1) (Matrix.of fun (ri qj : ι × n b) ↦
      ∑ k, X k * C (ψ b (Θ (e.symm k) ri.1 qj.1) ri.2 qj.2)).det =
      (comp ι ι (n b) (n b) O ((Θ b).map (ψ b))).det := by
    rw [eval_det_generic]
    congr 4
    simp [Pi.single_apply, Finset.sum_ite_eq']
  have hF0 (b : B) : (Matrix.of fun (ri qj : ι × n b) ↦
      ∑ k, X k * C (ψ b (Θ (e.symm k) ri.1 qj.1) ri.2 qj.2)).det ≠ 0 := fun h ↦ htop b <| by
    rw [← hdet b, ← hF b, h, map_zero, AddValuation.map_zero]
  choose c G hFG hG using fun b ↦ exists_eq_C_pow_mul_isUnit_coeff hϖ (hF0 b)
  refine ⟨Θ, c, G, hΘ, hG, hFG, fun b ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [← hdet b, ← hF b, hFG b, map_mul, eval_C, addVal_mul, addVal_pow,
    addVal_uniformizer hϖ, nsmul_one]
  exact le_self_add

omit [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n] [DecidableEq ι] [IsDomain O] [IsDiscreteValuationRing O]
  [IsFractionRing O K] in
/-- If some `Sol_b` has infinite length, the sum of their lengths is infinite. -/
private theorem le_sum_length_blockSolutions_of_eq_top {B : Type*} [Fintype B] {n : B → Type*}
    [∀ b, Fintype (n b)] [∀ b, DecidableEq (n b)] (ψ : ∀ b, 𝒜 →ₐ[O] Matrix (n b) (n b) O)
    (Rel : Submodule 𝒜 (ι → 𝒜)) {b : B}
    (hb : Module.length O (blockSolutions (ψ b) Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) = ⊤)
    (x : ℕ∞) :
    x ≤ ∑ b, Module.length O (blockSolutions (ψ b) Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) :=
  le_top.trans (hb.symm.trans_le (Finset.single_le_sum (f := fun b ↦ Module.length O
    (blockSolutions (ψ b) Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K)))) (fun _ _ ↦ zero_le)
    (Finset.mem_univ b)))

omit [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n] in
/-- **Lengths from generic determinants of block homomorphisms.** Let `ψ_b : 𝒜 → M_{n_b}(O)` (`b ∈
B`, finitely many) be surjective and `Rel ⊆ 𝒜^ι` a left `𝒜`-submodule. If an ideal `J ⊆ O` contains
every coefficient of `∏_b det ψ_b(∑_k X_k Θ_k) ∈ O[X_1, …, X_m]`, for every `m` and all arrays `Θ_k`
with rows in `Rel`, then `length_O(O/J) ≤ ∑_b length_O Sol_b`. -/
theorem length_quot_le_sum_length_blockSolutions {B : Type*} [Fintype B] {n : B → Type*}
    [∀ b, Fintype (n b)] [∀ b, DecidableEq (n b)] (ψ : ∀ b, 𝒜 →ₐ[O] Matrix (n b) (n b) O)
    (hψ : ∀ b, Function.Surjective (ψ b)) (Rel : Submodule 𝒜 (ι → 𝒜)) (J : Ideal O)
    (hJ : ∀ (m : ℕ) (Θ : Fin m → Matrix ι ι 𝒜), (∀ k r, Θ k r ∈ Rel) →
      ∀ s, (∏ b, (Matrix.of fun (ri qj : ι × n b) ↦
        ∑ k, X k * C (ψ b (Θ k ri.1 qj.1) ri.2 qj.2)).det).coeff s ∈ J) :
    Module.length O (O ⧸ J) ≤
      ∑ b, Module.length O (blockSolutions (ψ b) Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) := by
  classical
  by_cases htop : ∃ b, Module.length O
      (blockSolutions (ψ b) Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) = ⊤
  · obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := htop
    exact le_sum_length_blockSolutions_of_eq_top ψ Rel hb _
  push Not at htop
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := exists_irreducible O
  obtain ⟨Θ, c, G, hΘ, hG, hFG, hc⟩ := exists_generic_factorization ψ hψ Rel hϖ htop
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := IsLocalRing.exists_isUnit_coeff_prod Finset.univ fun b _ ↦ hG b
  have hmem := hJ _ (fun k ↦ Θ ((Fintype.equivFin B).symm k)) (fun k r ↦ hΘ _ r) t
  simp_rw [hFG] at hmem
  rw [Finset.prod_mul_distrib, ← map_prod, Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum, coeff_C_mul] at hmem
  calc Module.length O (O ⧸ J) ≤ ((∑ b, c b : ℕ) : ℕ∞) :=
        length_quotient_le_of_pow_mul_mem hϖ ht hmem
    _ ≤ _ := by
        push_cast
        exact Finset.sum_le_sum fun b _ ↦ hc b

omit [Fintype n] [IsDomain O] [IsDiscreteValuationRing O] in
/-- A factor `G` of a generic block determinant `det ψ(∑_k X_k Θ_k) = C a * G`, `a ≠ 0`, has total
degree at most the size `#ι · #n` of the block matrix. -/
private theorem totalDegree_le_of_eq_C_mul_det [Fintype n] [IsDomain O]
    (ψ : 𝒜 →ₐ[O] Matrix n n O) {m : ℕ} (Θ : Fin m → Matrix ι ι 𝒜) {a : O} (ha : a ≠ 0)
    {G : MvPolynomial (Fin m) O}
    (hG : (Matrix.of fun (ri qj : ι × n) ↦ ∑ k, X k * C (ψ (Θ k ri.1 qj.1) ri.2 qj.2)).det =
      C a * G) :
    G.totalDegree ≤ Fintype.card (ι × n) := by
  rw [← totalDegree_C_mul_eq ha, ← hG]
  refine (totalDegree_det_le fun ri qj ↦ ?_).trans_eq (mul_one _)
  rw [Matrix.of_apply]
  refine (totalDegree_finsetSum _ _).trans (Finset.sup_le fun k _ ↦ ?_)
  refine (totalDegree_mul _ _).trans ?_
  rw [totalDegree_C, add_zero]
  exact TauCeti.totalDegree_X_le k

omit [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n] in
/-- **One array over a large residue field.** In the setting of
`TauCeti.length_quot_le_sum_length_blockSolutions`, if the residue field of `O` has more than `#ι ·
∑_b n_b` elements, an ideal `J` containing `∏_b det ψ_b(Θ)` for every single array `Θ` with rows in
`Rel` satisfies `length_O(O/J) ≤ ∑_b length_O Sol_b`. -/
theorem length_quot_le_sum_length_blockSolutions_of_card_residueField {B : Type*} [Fintype B]
    {n : B → Type*} [∀ b, Fintype (n b)] [∀ b, DecidableEq (n b)]
    (ψ : ∀ b, 𝒜 →ₐ[O] Matrix (n b) (n b) O) (hψ : ∀ b, Function.Surjective (ψ b))
    (Rel : Submodule 𝒜 (ι → 𝒜)) (J : Ideal O)
    (hk : ((Fintype.card ι * ∑ b, Fintype.card (n b) : ℕ) : Cardinal) <
      Cardinal.mk (IsLocalRing.ResidueField O))
    (hJ : ∀ Θ : Matrix ι ι 𝒜, (∀ r, Θ r ∈ Rel) →
      ∏ b, (comp ι ι (n b) (n b) O (Θ.map (ψ b))).det ∈ J) :
    Module.length O (O ⧸ J) ≤
      ∑ b, Module.length O (blockSolutions (ψ b) Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) := by
  classical
  by_cases htop : ∃ b, Module.length O
      (blockSolutions (ψ b) Rel (K ⧸ range (Algebra.linearMap O K))) = ⊤
  · obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := htop
    exact le_sum_length_blockSolutions_of_eq_top ψ Rel hb _
  push Not at htop
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := exists_irreducible O
  obtain ⟨Θ, c, G, hΘ, hG, hFG, hc⟩ := exists_generic_factorization ψ hψ Rel hϖ htop
  set e := Fintype.equivFin B
  -- The reduction of `∏_b G_b` is a nonzero polynomial of small degree over the residue field.
  have hP : map (IsLocalRing.residue O) (∏ b, G b) ≠ 0 := by
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := IsLocalRing.exists_isUnit_coeff_prod Finset.univ fun b _ ↦ hG b
    intro h
    refine (IsLocalRing.residue_ne_zero_iff_isUnit _).2 ht ?_
    simp [← coeff_map, h]
  have hdegG (b : B) : (G b).totalDegree ≤ Fintype.card (ι × n b) :=
    totalDegree_le_of_eq_C_mul_det (ψ b) _ (pow_ne_zero _ hϖ.ne_zero) (hFG b)
  have hdeg : (map (IsLocalRing.residue O) (∏ b, G b)).totalDegree ≤
      Fintype.card ι * ∑ b, Fintype.card (n b) := by
    calc (map (IsLocalRing.residue O) (∏ b, G b)).totalDegree ≤ (∏ b, G b).totalDegree :=
          Finset.sup_mono (support_map_subset (IsLocalRing.residue O) _)
      _ ≤ ∑ b, (G b).totalDegree := totalDegree_finsetProd _ _
      _ ≤ ∑ b, Fintype.card (ι × n b) := Finset.sum_le_sum fun b _ ↦ hdegG b
      _ = _ := by simp [Fintype.card_prod, Finset.mul_sum]
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := exists_eval_ne_zero_of_totalDegree_lt_card hP
    (lt_of_le_of_lt (by exact_mod_cast hdeg) hk)
  choose a' ha' using fun k ↦ IsLocalRing.residue_surjective (a k)
  -- The array `Θ = ∑_k a'_k Θ_k` is optimal for every block at once.
  have hmem := hJ (∑ k, a' k • Θ (e.symm k)) fun r ↦ by
    have hr : (∑ k, a' k • Θ (e.symm k)) r = ∑ k, a' k • Θ (e.symm k) r := by
      funext q
      simp [Matrix.sum_apply]
    rw [hr]
    exact Rel.sum_mem fun k _ ↦ Rel.smul_of_tower_mem (a' k) (hΘ _ r)
  simp_rw [← eval_det_generic, hFG, ← map_prod, Finset.prod_mul_distrib, ← map_prod,
    Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum, map_mul, eval_C] at hmem
  have hu : IsUnit (eval a' (∏ b, G b)) := by
    have hra : (IsLocalRing.residue O) ∘ a' = a := funext ha'
    rw [← IsLocalRing.residue_ne_zero_iff_isUnit, eval₂_comp, hra, ← eval_map]
    exact ha
  calc Module.length O (O ⧸ J) ≤ ((∑ b, c b : ℕ) : ℕ∞) :=
        length_quotient_le_of_pow_mul_mem hϖ hu hmem
    _ ≤ _ := by
        push_cast
        exact Finset.sum_le_sum fun b _ ↦ hc b

end Generic

end TauCeti
